Package: Pando
Version: 2.0.9
Type: Package
Title: Inferring regulomes from multi-modal single-cell genomics data
Authors@R: person(given = "Jonas Simon",
               family = "Fleck",
               role = c("aut", "cre"),
               email = "jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch",
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4686-7254"))
Maintainer: Jonas Simon Fleck <jonas.fleck@bsse.ethz.ch>
Description: Pando jointly uses scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq measurements to infer
    regulatory relationships between TF-binding site pairs and target genes.
    For two or more conditions within a broad cell type, infer_condition_grn
    retains the original Pando regulatory-domain, motif, peak-target-correlation
    and TF-target-correlation candidate logic while producing condition-
    comparable coefficients. Candidate discovery is run on all eligible-
    condition cells pooled together and independently within each condition.
    Exact target-TF-region triples passing both configured correlation gates in
    the pooled/global calculation or in at least one condition are deduplicated
    into one frozen common dictionary. Every condition is fitted once on this
    identical ordered dictionary with the original TF-by-ATAC interaction
    predictor and ordinary ridge regularization. Conditions share the predictor
    dictionary, equal-condition within-condition RMS scaling convention, and one
    target-specific cross-validated lambda, but coefficients are not fused or
    shrunk toward coefficients from other conditions. Ridge keeps the penalized
    system identifiable under severe collinearity and raw rank deficiency while
    preserving directly comparable condition coefficient coordinates. Robust
    approximate ridge-Wald P values are BH adjusted within condition. An edge is
    active when its condition-specific coefficient is estimable and BH-supported
    and the exact edge has either pooled/global or that condition's local Pando
    candidate support. Global support therefore protects dictionary admission
    against unstable small-condition marginal correlations but cannot activate a
    condition edge without condition-specific ridge evidence. Active
    penalty_effect values are projected as beta times RNA(TF) times ATAC(peak).
    Pairwise condition contrasts are computed directly from the no-fusion ridge
    covariance. Coefficient and contrast P values remain approximate and
    conditional on data-dependent candidate discovery and CV-selected ridge
    regularization. Standard infer_grn retains the original Gaussian GLM as its
    default method and additionally supports single-task ridge. Target-parallel
    candidate discovery and ridge fitting use target-specific payload batches,
    and independent cell-type jobs can be dispatched through BiocParallel.
